data/ folder contains the churn data, and the data has been splitted to initial and retrain... 
its for train the model with initial data first... 
and use the retrain data for retrain the model after detecting the data drift

mlflow:
    mlflow saves and registers all trained model... but, it promotes to production only when the model meet 80% acc.
    currently, model saves as the name='Logistic_model', but, it registers as 'CustomerChurnModel'.

the project has arrived till monitoring..

what did on this project:
    - splitted og data to initial and retrain data.
    - versioned data using the dvc.
    - trained the LogisticRegression model and tracked experiments using mlflow.
    - all trained models are logged and registered into mlflow. but, only the model which passes above 80% accuaracy are 
      maded to production.. used mlflow alias for that.
    - used fastapi to make it an application.
    - used docker to package the application.
    - implemented ci for test the api, python, dockerizing.
    - hosted mlflow server on dagshub. so, whenever i train a better model and it passes the threshold, the application 
      could load the production model directly from the mlflow.sklearn.
    - deployed the application on render. hosted mlflow connected to app using dagshub library. application deployed to 
      render after passing the ci tests.
    - used prometheus and grafana for monitoring. used their official image on docker to use the prometheus and grafana.
    - created three metrics (high api latency, API Error rate, Total API requests).
    - created alertness for each metric. and setted the gmail for contact point.